Extract @Translation annotations that carry an arguments parameter.

Filed upstream as https://www.drupal.org/project/potx/issues/3615813.

The annotation pattern only allowed an optional "context" parameter after the
string, then required the closing parenthesis. Any other parameter made the
match fail, so the string was not extracted at all - and potx then reported it
as "In @Translation, only one, non-empty static string is allowed in double
quotes", which is misleading since the syntax is valid.

The common case is "arguments", used for placeholders:

  description = @Translation("A string provided by <a href=':google'>Google</a>.",
    arguments = { ":google" = "https://www.google.com/" }),

Both "arguments" and "context" are documented parameters of the Translation
annotation, so this is a genuine upstream bug rather than a local need. In our
codebase it cost the Danish translations of roughly a dozen metatag field
descriptions.

The replacement allows any number of "key = value" parameters on either side of
an optional context, and keeps the capture group numbering the code below
depends on: 1 is the message, 3 is the quoted context.

diff --git a/potx.inc b/potx.inc
--- a/potx.inc
+++ b/potx.inc
@@ -2307,7 +2307,18 @@
       // Match for a possible empty string too, so we can signal that kind of
       // error in our standard way (from the save callback), instead of
       // signaling a generic error from here around syntax.
-      preg_match_all('!\s*@Translation\(\s*"([^"]*)"(\s*,\s*context\s*=\s*("[^"]+"))?\s*\)!', $string, $found);
+      // Annotations may carry parameters besides context - most commonly
+      // arguments, used for placeholders in for example metatag descriptions.
+      // Allow any number of those on either side of an optional context, so
+      // that the string is still extracted. The delimiter is "~" rather than
+      // "!" because the negative lookahead below contains "!".
+      $other_parameter = '(?:\s*,\s*(?!context\s*=)[a-zA-Z_]+\s*=\s*(?:\{[^{}]*\}|"[^"]*"))';
+      $pattern = '~\s*@Translation\(\s*"([^"]*)"'
+        . $other_parameter . '*'
+        . '(\s*,\s*context\s*=\s*("[^"]+"))?'
+        . $other_parameter . '*'
+        . '\s*\)~';
+      preg_match_all($pattern, $string, $found);
       if (isset($found) && is_array($found) && count($found[1])) {

         foreach ($found[1] as $index => $match) {
